-- title:
--   Vieta relation U²-S U+π=0 in the crossing model
-- statement:
--   Let $W$ be a commutative ring and let $\pi \in W$. Work in the crossing model $R_\pi =$ `UVCrossingModel W π`, namely the quotient of the ring $W[[X_0,X_1]]$ of formal power series in two variables indexed by `Fin 2` by the ideal generated by the single element $X_0X_1 - \pi$, where $\pi$ is viewed in the power series ring through the constant-coefficient map. In this quotient one has the element `const π π`, the class of the constant power series $\pi$, and the three distinguished elements `U π`, `V π` and `S π`, the last of which is by definition the sum `U π + V π`; the class `U π * V π` equals `const π π`. The assertion is the Vieta identity in $R_\pi$: $$(U\pi)^2 - (S\pi)\,(U\pi) + \mathrm{const}\,\pi\,\pi = 0,$$ i.e. `U π` is a root of the monic quadratic $T^2 - (S\pi)T + \mathrm{const}\,\pi\,\pi$ whose coefficients are the trace and the norm of the pair $(U\pi, V\pi)$. No hypothesis beyond commutativity of $W$ is imposed; in particular $\pi$ is an arbitrary element, possibly a unit or zero.
--
--   This is the local Vieta relation exhibiting the crossing model $W[[u,v]]/(uv-\pi)$ as generated by a root of a monic quadratic over the subring generated by the symmetric functions $s = u+v$ and $\pi = uv$ — the local picture, at a supersingular point, of a degree-two cover branched where $u = v$. It is used by [`ModularCurve.UVCrossingModel.exists_ringEquiv_adjoinRoot`](thm.html#ModularCurve.UVCrossingModel.exists_ringEquiv_adjoinRoot) and [`ModularCurve.UVCrossingModel.exists_ringEquiv_adjoinRoot_of_isPrecomplete`](thm.html#ModularCurve.UVCrossingModel.exists_ringEquiv_adjoinRoot_of_isPrecomplete), which build from it ring isomorphisms of the crossing model with an `AdjoinRoot` construction.
